  "description": "Pan-seared pork chops served with spinach and a rich, sweet peach sauce make up this simple, seasonal one-pot meal.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: bone-in rib → center-cut chops\n\nNotes: When buying peaches for this recipe and for grilling, you want to make sure that they aren't overly ripe as they will completely fall apart during the cooking process. You don't want ones that feel like baseballs either, as they will not be sweet enough. Instead, feel for ones that give slightly when squeezed.",
